{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 520 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D6"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Dacarbazine has been on FDA's shortage list since 2021-10-20 and remains listed as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our 10 mg/mL, 10 mL vials at Corvale General and Corvale East are labeled to Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC (FEI 1450022).",
      "cites": ["E2", "E4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1123748 at that plant ended 2020-05-18 and was classified OAI, with the classification letter dated 2024-05-22, 520 days before the shortage posting on 2021-10-20.",
      "cites": ["D6", "E12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A second OAI inspection (1174894) ended 2022-06-30, 253 days after the posting, and a VAI inspection (1216183) ended 2023-08-24.",
      "cites": ["D7", "D8", "E13", "E14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 2.9 days of the 10 mg/mL presentation on hand while Corvale General has 15.8 days.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑ranked first option is to transfer 5 vials of 10 mg/mL, 10 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East to about 4 days on hand while Corvale General retains roughly two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Alternate options include purchasing from Meitheal Pharmaceuticals Inc. (not on FDA's shortage list) or using Hikma's 200 mg vial with pharmacist verification.",
      "cites": ["D13", "D14", "E6", "E16"]
    }
  ]
}
